      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "The Andean flamingos — two species restricted to the high-altitude salt flats and lakes of the Andes Mountains in South America. They are the rarest flamingos, both classified as Vulnerable. They endure extreme conditions including intense UV radiation and nightly freezing temperatures at elevations over 4,000 metres.",
